**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** A saved scene persists as its own kit file, `<scene name>.setup-json`, in today's `Scene.SceneSnapshot` shape (001 §A 'Kit extensions … .setup-json'; the S4.3 brief: a scene is <scene name>.setup-json, in today's Scene.SceneSnapshot shape, which S8.2 replaces with slots). The stack is step 146's. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Scene.fs`, which opens `LibraryEntryFiles` (step 24); each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S4.3. (a) `SceneName` (`Scene.fs:SceneName`) gains `member this.fileStem : FileStem`, `FileStem.ofText this.value`: the name keeps the lab's characters and only the characters Windows forbids become `_` (.spec-md §3.11, step 24's one rule). (b) `SceneSnapshot` (`Scene.fs:SceneSnapshot`) gains `member this.libraryReferences : EntryReference list` (step 137): the `placement.valueId` of each element that names a library entry (`ElementValueId.tryToLibraryEntryId`, step 24) as an `EntryLatestReference`, in element order, each once; an unbound element and a value id that names no entry give none. It is what a kit snapshots when it records the scene (step 149). (c) After `SceneSnapshot`: `SceneFile = { schemaVersion : FileSchemaVersion; name : SceneName; scene : SceneSnapshot }`, the `.setup-json`, with `static member currentSchemaVersion : FileSchemaVersion` = 1. The name is kept inside the file because the file stem is the name made filesystem-safe and can differ from it. (2) Schema. New `OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/setup.schema.json`, draft 2020-12, `$id` `https://berreman/schema/setup.json`. `schemaVersion` is a positive integer, checked unconditionally. Only under `if` it is 1: the root holds exactly `schemaVersion`, `name` (a string holding a non-white-space character, the pattern `\S`) and `scene`; `scene` holds exactly `elements` (an array), `view`, `snap` and `pivot`; their shapes are bound by the serializer. It is a `Content` item copied `PreserveNewest` beside `schema/experiment.schema.json`, with no comment. `SchemaValidation.fs` gains `validateSceneFile (element : JsonElement) : Result<unit, StorageError>` over `validateWith`, its schema loaded once behind a `lazy`. (3) `KitContentFiles.fs` (step 146): `type SceneFile with member this.fileText : Result<KitFileText, StorageError>` (`nodeOf` rendered by `canonicalFileText`) and `type KitFileText with member this.parseSceneFile : Result<SceneFile, StorageError>` = `parseVersionedText validateSceneFile SetupKitFile.extension SceneFile.currentSchemaVersion this.value`. Tests, in `KitContentFileJsonTests` (step 146). Its fixture scene is written as a record, as `SceneRoundTripTests.fs` writes its source model's elements: a light source bound to the 600 nm source preset (`PresetIds.source600`), a linear polarizer bound to the linear-polarizer preset, a detector that is unbound and sits on the polarizer's reflected beam, a view panned and zoomed off `Table.defaultView`, `SnapToBeam` and `PivotAtIncidentFace`. `a scene is stored under its name made filesystem-safe`: `SceneName "CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL"` has the file stem of the same text, `SceneName "a: b/c"` has `FileStem "a_ b_c"`, and `SetupKitFile.fileNameOf` of the first is `FileName "CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL.setup-json"`. `a setup file round-trips through its canonical text`: a `SceneFile` of `SceneName "Bench: A"` and the fixture, by `fileText` and `parseSceneFile`, answers an equal file; the text holds no `\r`, ends with exactly one `\n`, lists its top-level keys as `name`, `scene`, `schemaVersion`, and writing the parsed file again gives the same text. `a setup file of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`: the text with `schemaVersion` set to 2, with its body intact and alone, answers `UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr` with `fileExtension = SetupKitFile.extension`, `found = FileSchemaVersion 2` and `expected = FileSchemaVersion 1`. `a schema-invalid or malformed setup file is refused before it binds`: the text without `name`, with `name` set to `"   "`, with `scene` lacking `pivot`, and with an extra top-level key, each answer `SchemaValidationErr` with messages; `{` answers `MalformedJsonErr`. `a scene references the library entries its elements bind, each once, at their latest`: the fixture's `libraryReferences` is exactly the `EntryLatestReference`s of the source preset's and the linear-polarizer preset's GUIDs, in that order; a scene binding the source preset twice references it once; and a scene of unbound elements references nothing.

**Acceptance.** After the setup file lands, `SceneFile.fileText` MUST render canonical JSON that `KitFileText.parseSceneFile` reads back equal, validated against `schema/setup.schema.json`, another schema version being `UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`, `SceneName.fileStem` MUST keep the lab's characters, and `SceneSnapshot.libraryReferences` MUST name each bound entry once; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a scene is stored under its name made filesystem-safe`, `a setup file round-trips through its canonical text`, `a setup file of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`, `a schema-invalid or malformed setup file is refused before it binds`, `a scene references the library entries its elements bind, each once, at their latest`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the eleven s17 invariants MUST pass.
